title The keyword that split a family in two
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, deep-read one council-rota row, Standfast on reds, send the finished increment
think Council rota row 0 (Aether - Jupiter) read: follow-our-compass, the Lindy effect, the grain and the crossing. The Lindy piece carried the lap -- a meter read thousands of times over years earns its correction more than a body lifted once.
think Standfast on the way in: era suite GREEN at 12 and the Caravan choir GREEN at 108 before any constructive work, and every REDS row from 137 to 143 already closed. The line was clear.
think elder_waits led the queue at 504 by the prior lap's recommend, so I read the family by hand before lifting it, the same way REDS %140 was found.
think The scan reported 53 declared and 43 identical. Reading the other ten showed eight writing the same fifteen-line body under a private fn rather than pub fn, byte for byte apart from that one word.
think Both meters hash a body by its own exact text with the signature included, so the visibility keyword sits inside the key. One rule written in fifty-one rungs read as two families of forty-three and eight.
think Measured the whole size before booking: stripping a leading pub from every line and re-running the carry grouping gave 63,964 against the meter's 63,852, so 112 carried lines stood outside a ceiling whose whole job is to count them, across fifteen split families.
think Then found the lantern had already fired. The carry scan's own doc block named this exact split for fill_table a lap earlier and closed by asking the reader to read past the queue. A caution a reader must remember is a blindness with a label on it, so the note became a check.
think Fixed all three windows rather than two -- the carry grouping, the reach family hash, and the reach sink window, which was worse still because it read pub fn alone and could not see a private duplicated body at all.
think The sink correction was the largest: foreclosure 235 to 1,140 against a corpus 61,873 to 69,379. A rung the harness imports forecloses nearly five times what the arc believed, which makes the one-way fold-line door dearer than every lap of this arc has priced it.
think Rows 140-141 folded to crux/archive/ before booking %144, since the living pin stood at 24,378 bytes against its 24,576 bound.
obs The correction found cost rather than freedom, and that is the evidence it is a correction rather than a manufactured win. elder_waits reads fifty-one identical bodies where it read forty-three, and the five extra rungs above the fold line each keep their own Table private -- so folding them would publish a record type five rungs chose to keep, and the honest lift still leaves those five at home. may_pass, choose_pass, sibling_waits, door_admits, finding_path, load_one, and read_own_line all stand exactly where they stood.
obs The carry ceiling rose rather than fell, against a ratchet whose discipline is that it only ever comes down. That is named in the ledger, in the witness GREEN line, and on the operator card, because a rise nobody explains reads as carry coming back.
obs Two prose guards fired on this lap's own new sentences and both were right -- the recited-count guard named four superseded numbers with no assert holding them, and each sentence was rewritten to name the shape rather than loosened to admit the number.
obs No body was lifted this lap. A meter repaired is Lindy-heavier than a family folded: the queue this meter orders will choose every remaining lift of the arc.
